From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] wordcraft-web: window.__hostFinalCopy(), the parent's synchronous pull of the unsaved document as it closes

The document server's wrapper page closes the session in its own pagehide (the host removed it: HRM's Back runs destroyEditor() and empties the container at once). That pagehide runs before this page's, so a postMessage handover from here reaches a parent already gone, and an edit made in the last 3 s (before the debounced autosave) was lost (status 4). Now the bridge sets window.__hostFinalCopy(): the wrapper calls it synchronously and sends the bytes in its keepalive close. It returns the document as the autosave would send it when it has unsaved changes not handed over yet, else null (clean, read only, already handed over), and counts as a handover so the autosave does not send the same state again. The web shell implements App::as_any_mut so the closure reaches the app through WebRunner::app_mut.

---

diff --git a/apps/wordcraft-web/src/autosave.rs b/apps/wordcraft-web/src/autosave.rs
index 55b21969..24060d81 100644
--- a/apps/wordcraft-web/src/autosave.rs
+++ b/apps/wordcraft-web/src/autosave.rs
@@ -44,6 +44,11 @@ impl Debounce {
         self.last_sent = Some(now);
     }
 
+    /// Revision `rev` was handed over already.
+    pub fn was_sent(&self, rev: u64) -> bool {
+        self.sent == Some(rev)
+    }
+
     /// One frame of an unsaved, editable document at revision `rev`, `now` in milliseconds.
     pub fn tick(&mut self, rev: u64, now: f64) -> Tick {
         if self.sent == Some(rev) {
@@ -111,6 +116,7 @@ mod tests {
         d.reset();
         assert_eq!(d.tick(5, 10_000.0), Tick::Wait(3_000.0), "an unsaved document at the same revision is new again");
         d.mark_sent(5, 10_500.0);
+        assert!(d.was_sent(5) && !d.was_sent(6));
         assert_eq!(d.tick(5, 20_000.0), Tick::Idle);
     }
 }
